From 5522dfe96781efaf5f47d6e6af523450ebd1799b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:15:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(playback): cut the twin-able ops into a dense layer
 (S3b)

The playback worker gets an opt-in layer mode (PlayWorker::spawn_layered).
Each plain op whose tool (ball, flat end mill) and moves (linear, upright)
have an f32 twin is cut by a caller-given cutter into a dense cut layer
on the packed frame's lattice; the f64 field cuts every other op. A frame
is max(pack_cut(field), layer), always whole.

- camcraft-sim: LayerPlay (the layer as a function of the move count,
  its own keyframes, cut only for a picture), LayerCutter and the CPU
  twin law cutter (run_twin_items_onto), layer_tool (the display cut's
  tool law), twin_refusal, merge_max.
- camcraft-app: FieldPlay::set_layer / layer_frame / drop_layer; the cut
  dispatch moves to stock_play_cut.rs and the frame packing to
  stock_play_worker_frame.rs (400-line law). A layer fault turns the mode
  off and rebuilds the field with every op at the same position.
- camcraft-gpu: the spot check takes the margin of every item that ties
  with the result (a spring pass over a keyframe no longer refuses a good
  GPU layer); the device-loss Err of cut_into is pinned.

No caller turns the mode on yet (S3c: the GPU cutter on the render
device), so the product picture does not change. No new crate edge:
camcraft-app does not depend on camcraft-gpu (#3589, one wgpu instance).

Refs #2629

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
